TODO - Future Iterations
========================

  [ ] 1. Handle impl-before-class ordering
   - Currently: if an impl block appears before its class declaration in source code,
     SymTabCreationVisitor::visit(startNode&) reports "Missing Class Declaration"
     because the class hasn't been inserted into the global symbol table yet.
   - Fix: do a two-pass scan over startNode children:
       Pass 1: insert all classdecl entries into the global map
       Pass 2: process impldef entries (merging into already-registered classes)
   - This decouples source ordering from symbol resolution.
   - Location: visitor.cpp, SymTabCreationVisitor::visit(startNode&), ~line 148
  [ ] 2. Parameter types match declaration (in order): for each position,
         compare the impl param type to the decl param type.
         Note: param order matters; map lookup by name is not sufficient here —
         need to compare by position using an ordered list.


========================================================================
SEMANTIC CHECKS — planned for SemanticCheckingVisitor
========================================================================

Priority order — do in this sequence (later items depend on earlier ones):
  TIER 1 (foundation):  s, t
  TIER 2 (require s+t):  u, v, w, k(b), q
  TIER 3 (independent):  r, g, j, l, m, n

In visit(implNode&)    [implementation block checks]
------------------------------------------------------
  [x] a. Declared function exists: the function name being implemented
         must exist in the class's symbol table (classEntry->link).
  [x] b. Return type matches declaration: the returntype in the impl's
         funchead must equal the declared return type in the class.
  [x] c. Parameter count matches declaration: count params in impl's funchead
         against count in the corresponding class funcdecl entry's link map.
  [x] e. No duplicate implementations: the same class::function should not be
         implemented more than once. Track in a set<pair<className, funcName>>.

In visit(classNode&)   [class declaration checks]
--------------------------------------------------
  [ ] g. Inherited class exists: every id in the isalist must be found in the
         global symbol table as kind="class". Report error if not found.
         Access: iterate child with semanticMeaning=="isalist", check each id's nodeValue.
  [ ] h. No member name shadows inherited member (warning-level, optional).

In visit(startNode&)   [global-scope checks]
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  [ ] i. Every declared class has at least one implementation block.
         (Already done in SymTabCreationVisitor — may want to move/duplicate here.)
  [ ] j. Exactly one main function exists and its return type is void.
  [ ] r. Circular class dependency: build a directed graph where edge A→B means
         class A has a data member of type B or inherits from B. Run DFS/Kahn's
         cycle detection. For each cycle report:
         "circular class dependency involving <classA> and <classB>".
         Run after symbol table is fully built.

In visit(funcNode&)    [free function / main checks]
-----------------------------------------------------
  [ ] k. Return type consistency:
         (a) if returntype != "void", verify a return statement exists.
         (b) The type of the return expression must equal the declared return type.
             Requires expression type inference (item s) to be done first.
  [ ] l. No duplicate free function names at global scope.

In visit(vardeclNode&)  [local variable declaration checks]
------------------------------------------------------------
  [ ] m. If variable type is a class name (e.g. "LOCAL f1: LINEAR"), verify
         that class exists in global symbol table.
  [ ] n. If a constructor call (aparams) is present on the vardecl, verify:
           - the class has a declared constructor
           - argument count matches constructor parameter count
           - argument types match constructor parameter types
         Access: vardecl → dimlist → aparams children for the arguments.

In visit(aparamsandidNode&)   [function call checks]
----------------------------------------------------
  [ ] o. Called function exists in the current scope or class scope.
         Error: "use of undeclared free function <name>" or
                "use of undeclared member function <name>" depending on context.
  [ ] p. Argument count matches the declared parameter count.
  [ ] q. Argument types match declared parameter types.
         Requires expression type inference (item s) to be done first.
         Array parameters: check compatible dimensionality (item w).

In type inference pass   [expression type resolution — req 10, 11]
------------------------------------------------------------------
  ITEM s — Expression type inference (build bottom-up, one sub-step at a time)
  [ ] s1. Add `std::string inferredType` field to the AST node struct/class
          so any node can carry its resolved type.
  [ ] s2. Annotate literal nodes with fixed types:
            intlit   → inferredType = "integer"
            floatlit → inferredType = "float"
            stringlit → inferredType = "string"
  [ ] s3. Annotate identifier nodes: look up the identifier's name in the
          active scope chain; set inferredType to the declared type found,
          or leave blank/error if not found (error handling is item t1).
  [ ] s4. Annotate arithmetic expression nodes (+, -, *, /):
            int   op int   → "integer"
            float op float → "float"
            mixed          → emit "type mismatch in arithmetic expression"
                             and set inferredType = "error"
  [ ] s5. Annotate relational expression nodes (<, >, ==, !=, <=, >=):
            result is always "integer" (boolean-as-int convention).
  [ ] s6. Annotate function call nodes: look up the called function in the
          active scope/class table; set inferredType = declared return type.
  [ ] s7. Annotate dot-access nodes: after item v resolves the member,
          set inferredType = member's declared type (wired last, depends on v).

  ITEM t — Undeclared identifier errors (piggyback on s3/s6 walks)
  [ ] t1. In s3 (identifier lookup): if the name is not found in the scope
          chain, emit "use of undeclared variable <name>".
  [ ] t2. In s6 (function call lookup): if the free function is not found
          in the global table, emit "use of undeclared free function <name>".
  [ ] t3. In dot-RHS lookup (v3 below): if the member function is not found
          in the class table, emit "use of undeclared member function <name>".
  [ ] t4. Wherever a type name is used as a class reference (vardecl, param),
          check it exists in the global symbol table as kind="class"; emit
          "use of undeclared class <name>" if missing.

In visit(assignNode&)   [assignment statement checks — req 10]
--------------------------------------------------------------
  ITEM u — Assignment type checking (depends on s being complete)
  [ ] u1. In visit(assignNode&), call the type-inference helper on the LHS
          child to get lhsType.
  [ ] u2. Call the type-inference helper on the RHS child to get rhsType.
  [ ] u3. If lhsType != rhsType (and neither is "error"), emit:
          "type error in assignment: cannot assign <rhsType> to <lhsType>".

In visit(dotNode&)   ["." operator checks — req 15]
----------------------------------------------------
  ITEM v — Dot operator validation (depends on s3 for LHS type)
  [ ] v1. In visit(dotNode&), infer the type of the LHS child (call s3/s4
          helper); store as lhsType.
  [ ] v2. If lhsType is not a known class name, emit:
          "dot operator applied to non-class type <lhsType>".
          Set inferredType = "error" and return early.
  [ ] v3. Look up the RHS identifier name in the symbol table of the class
          named lhsType:
            - If a data member: set inferredType = member's declared type.
            - If a member function: set inferredType = function's return type.
            - If not found: emit the appropriate undeclared-member error
              (handled by t3).

In visit(arrayIndexNode&)   [array access checks — req 13]
----------------------------------------------------------
  ITEM w — Array dimension consistency (depends on s and t)
  [ ] w1. In visit(arrayIndexNode&), count the number of index expressions
          provided (children of the index-list node).
  [ ] w2. Look up the declared dimension count for the array identifier from
          its symbol table entry.
  [ ] w3. If counts differ, emit:
          "wrong number of dimensions for array <name>: expected <n>, got <m>".
  [ ] w4. For each index expression, check inferredType == "integer"; if not,
          emit "array index must be of integer type, got <type>".
  [ ] w5. When an array is passed as a function argument, compare its
          declared dimensionality to the parameter's declared dimensionality;
          emit "incompatible array dimensionality for parameter <name>"
          if they differ.

In visit(funcNode&) / visit(implNode&)   [return-type expression check]
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
  ITEM k(b) — Return expression type must match declared return type
              (depends on s; complement to the already-done count check)
  [ ] kb1. Locate the return statement node inside the function body.
  [ ] kb2. Call the type-inference helper on the return expression child
           to get returnExprType.
  [ ] kb3. Compare returnExprType to the function's declared return type;
           if they differ, emit:
           "type error in return: expected <declaredType>, got <returnExprType>".

In visit(aparamsandidNode&)   [argument type checks — req 12]
-------------------------------------------------------------
  ITEM q — Argument types match declared parameter types (depends on s)
  [ ] q1. For each argument expression in the call, call the type-inference
          helper to get its type; collect into an ordered list argTypes.
  [ ] q2. Retrieve the declared parameter types for the called function
          (ordered list from symbol table entry).
  [ ] q3. For each position i where argTypes[i] != paramTypes[i], emit:
          "type mismatch for argument <i+1> in call to <funcName>:
           expected <paramType>, got <argType>".

